         brute_force_approach="No meaningfully simpler approach -- you must visit every land cell at least once.",
         optimal_approach="For each unvisited land cell, BFS (or DFS) outward marking every connected land cell visited, counting one island per BFS started.",
         common_mistakes="Forgetting to check grid boundaries before visiting a neighbor (IndexError); mutating the grid without a separate visited set AND forgetting that counts as \"marking visited\" too (either approach works, but pick one consistently).",
