         description="Given a grid of heights where the Pacific Ocean touches the top and left edges and the Atlantic touches the bottom and right edges, water flows from a cell to an adjacent cell only if the adjacent cell's height is <= the current cell's height. Return the list of cells [r, c] from which water can reach BOTH oceans.",
         constraints='1 <= rows, cols <= 200.',
         function_signature='def pacific_atlantic(heights):',
         starter_code="def pacific_atlantic(heights):\n    # Flip the problem: instead of asking 'can water FROM this cell reach\n    # the ocean', run DFS OUTWARD from each ocean's border cells, moving\n    # to a neighbor whenever the neighbor's height is >= the current\n    # height (water could have flowed the other way). A cell reachable\n    # from BOTH oceans this way is part of the answer.\n    pass\n",
