         common_mistakes="Using DFS instead of BFS -- DFS can find A path but has no guarantee of finding the SHORTEST one without extra bookkeeping, defeating the point of the problem; forgetting to check end_word is even present in the word list up front (if it's absent, no sequence can ever reach it, and it's a wasted search to not check this first); not marking a word visited immediately upon enqueueing it (only marking on dequeue can cause the same word to be enqueued multiple times from different neighbors).",
